---
import PhotoIntro from '../../components/PhotoIntro.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RevenueFlowFigure from '../../components/figures/RevenueFlowFigure.astro';

// 2026-10-20: 日本語トップ（src/pages/index.astro）と同じ見た目に揃えた。
// 読者は日本で売上をつくる海外企業の担当者なので、メッセージは Japan GTM が主、Revenue CRM は2本目の入口。
import NewsLatest from '../../components/NewsLatest.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Japan Revenue Operations for English-Speaking Leaders | Consilegy"
  description="We help English-speaking leaders in Japan and APAC build the CRM structure, revenue architecture, and GTM operations that make Japan execution visible and repeatable."
  lang="en"
  alternateUrl="/"
>
<link
  rel="preload"
  as="image"
  href="/images/common/hero-visual.webp"
  type="image/webp"
  fetchpriority="high"
  slot="head"
/>

<!-- ===================== HERO（左＝見出しとCTA、右＝入口2つ） ===================== -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="container hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="hero-eyebrow">For English-speaking leaders running Japan and APAC revenue</p>
      <h1>
        Make Japan revenue execution
        <span class="hero-accent">visible, manageable, and repeatable.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">
        A Japan GTM partner that starts from CRM, marketing, and sales operations, not market-entry slides.
        We design for how Japan actually buys, then build it into your stack, or into Revenue CRM, our own product.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--cta btn--lg">Contact Us</a>
        <a href="/en/crm/" class="btn btn--hero-outline btn--lg">See Revenue CRM →</a>
      </div>
      <p class="hero-proof"><strong>40+</strong> CRM / MA / SFA implementations<span class="hero-proof__sep">·</span>12 years B2B marketing in Japan<span class="hero-proof__sep">·</span>12 years in analytics</p>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-entries" aria-label="Which one is your company?">
      <a href="/en/services/" class="hero-entry">
        <span class="hero-entry__tag">CRM in place, not working</span>
        <span class="hero-entry__state">Salesforce, HubSpot, kintone, or Marketo is live. Sales doesn't log. Nobody trusts the dashboard.</span>
        <span class="hero-entry__cta">Redesign on the tools you have →</span>
        <span class="hero-entry__tools" aria-label="Platforms we work with">
          <span>Salesforce</span><span>HubSpot</span><span>kintone</span><span>Marketo</span><span>ServiceNow</span><span>Zoho CRM</span><span>Tableau / Looker</span>
        </span>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/crm/" class="hero-entry">
        <span class="hero-entry__tag">No CRM yet</span>
        <span class="hero-entry__state">Customer data lives in spreadsheets and inboxes. Deal status lives in people's heads.</span>
        <span class="hero-entry__cta">Revenue CRM, our own product →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<NewsLatest lang="en" />

<!-- ===================== PROBLEM（紺の帯：構造的な死角） ===================== -->
<section class="statement">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="statement-inner">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">The Structural Gap</p>
      <h2>Japan operations have a blind spot built in.</h2>
      <div class="statement-body">
        <p>Your CRM was configured for a different market. Pipeline stages, qualification criteria, and handoff rules don't match how Japanese buyers actually move.</p>
        <p>Your Japan team operates in Japanese. Every report that reaches you or HQ passes through an interpretation layer, and something gets lost.</p>
        <p>You can see the numbers. You cannot tell why Japan is underperforming, or where the system breaks. We build the revenue operations layer that makes Japan execution legible from both sides.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== HOW JAPAN BUYS（図） ===================== -->
<section class="band band--grey">
  <div class="container">
    <PhotoIntro subject="consultation" lang="en" priority={false}><header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">How Japan Buys</p>
      <h2>Most of the time is spent inside the buyer's company.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">Ringi, consensus, long waits. A pipeline built for a faster, single-decision-maker motion reads these weeks as "stalled". We design stages and metrics around them.</p>
    </header></PhotoIntro>
    <figure class="buy-figure" aria-labelledby="buy-figure-caption">
      <svg class="fig-pc" viewBox="0 0 1120 260" role="img" aria-label="How a Japanese B2B purchase moves: interest, internal consensus (ringi), approval, contract. Most time is spent in internal consensus." font-family="inherit">
        <defs><marker id="buy-arr" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#0F172A"/></marker></defs>
        <text x="40" y="24" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.5" fill="#64748b">BUYING PROCESS (EXAMPLE)</text>
        <!-- bracket over consensus -->
        <path d="M296 54 L296 44 L716 44 L716 54" fill="none" stroke="#3B82F6" stroke-width="2"/>
        <text x="506" y="36" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#2563EB" text-anchor="middle">Most time is spent here</text>
        <!-- stages -->
        <rect x="40" y="70" width="230" height="100" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
        
        <text x="60" y="100" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">STAGE 1</text>
        <text x="60" y="132" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Interest</text>
        <text x="60" y="156" font-size="16" fill="#475569">A champion engages</text>

        <rect x="296" y="70" width="420" height="100" rx="6" fill="#0F172A"/>
        <text x="316" y="100" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#CBD5E1">STAGE 2</text>
        <text x="316" y="132" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">Internal consensus (ringi)</text>
        <text x="316" y="156" font-size="16" fill="#E2E8F0">Stakeholders align, documents circulate</text>

        <rect x="742" y="70" width="160" height="100" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
        
        <text x="760" y="100" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">STAGE 3</text>
        <text x="760" y="132" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Approval</text>
        <text x="760" y="156" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Sign-off</text>

        <rect x="928" y="70" width="152" height="100" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
        
        <text x="946" y="100" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">STAGE 4</text>
        <text x="946" y="132" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Contract</text>
        <text x="946" y="156" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Start</text>

        <line x1="272" y1="120" x2="292" y2="120" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#buy-arr)"/>
        <line x1="718" y1="120" x2="738" y2="120" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#buy-arr)"/>
        <line x1="904" y1="120" x2="924" y2="120" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#buy-arr)"/>

        <!-- time bar -->
        <text x="40" y="214" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">TIME</text>
        <rect x="100" y="202" width="170" height="16" rx="3" fill="#E2E8F0"/>
        <rect x="296" y="202" width="420" height="16" rx="3" fill="#2563EB"/>
        <rect x="742" y="202" width="160" height="16" rx="3" fill="#E2E8F0"/>
        <rect x="928" y="202" width="152" height="16" rx="3" fill="#E2E8F0"/>
        <text x="40" y="248" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Bar lengths are illustrative. Measure the wait, not only the conversion rate.</text>
      </svg>
<svg class="fig-sp" viewBox="0 0 360 634" role="img" aria-label="How a Japanese B2B purchase moves: interest, internal consensus (ringi), approval, contract. Most time is spent in internal consensus." font-family="inherit">
        <defs><marker id="buy-arr-sp" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z" fill="#0F172A"/></marker></defs>
        <text x="0" y="22" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.5" fill="#64748b">BUYING PROCESS (EXAMPLE)</text>
        <text x="0" y="50" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">TIME</text>
        <rect x="0" y="64" width="12" height="94" rx="3" fill="#E2E8F0"/>
        <rect x="28" y="64" width="316" height="94" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
        <text x="46" y="92" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">STAGE 1</text>
        <text x="46" y="120" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Interest</text>
        <text x="46" y="144" font-size="16" fill="#475569">A champion engages</text>
        <line x1="186" y1="162" x2="186" y2="180" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#buy-arr-sp)"/>
        <text x="28" y="204" font-size="16" font-weight="600" fill="#2563EB">Most time is spent here</text>
        <rect x="0" y="214" width="12" height="116" rx="3" fill="#2563EB"/>
        <rect x="28" y="214" width="316" height="116" rx="6" fill="#0F172A"/>
        <text x="46" y="242" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#CBD5E1">STAGE 2</text>
        <text x="46" y="270" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#fff">Internal consensus (ringi)</text>
        <text x="46" y="294" font-size="16" fill="#E2E8F0">Stakeholders align,</text>
        <text x="46" y="316" font-size="16" fill="#E2E8F0">documents circulate</text>
        <line x1="186" y1="334" x2="186" y2="352" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#buy-arr-sp)"/>
        <rect x="0" y="358" width="12" height="94" rx="3" fill="#E2E8F0"/>
        <rect x="28" y="358" width="316" height="94" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
        <text x="46" y="386" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">STAGE 3</text>
        <text x="46" y="414" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Approval</text>
        <text x="46" y="438" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Sign-off</text>
        <line x1="186" y1="456" x2="186" y2="474" stroke="#0F172A" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#buy-arr-sp)"/>
        <rect x="0" y="480" width="12" height="94" rx="3" fill="#E2E8F0"/>
        <rect x="28" y="480" width="316" height="94" rx="6" fill="#fff" stroke="#E2E8F0"/>
        <text x="46" y="508" font-size="14" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#64748b">STAGE 4</text>
        <text x="46" y="536" font-size="20" font-weight="600" fill="#0F172A">Contract</text>
        <text x="46" y="560" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Start</text>
        <text x="0" y="604" font-size="16" fill="#475569">Bar lengths are illustrative. Measure</text>
        <text x="0" y="626" font-size="16" fill="#475569">the wait, not only the conversion rate.</text>
      </svg>
      <figcaption id="buy-figure-caption">In Japan, the longest stage often has no visible activity in your CRM. We add the wait time to the metrics so leadership can see it.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== USE CASES（3枚のカード） ===================== -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Who We Work With</p>
      <h2>Three situations we know well</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--three">
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">01</p>
        <h3>CRM built for a different market</h3>
        <p>You have a CRM. It was configured globally, or for a Western sales motion. Lead stages don't match Japan's buying cycle, and forecast data is unreliable. Your Japan team uses the system, but not in a way that produces real visibility.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">02</p>
        <h3>Japan pipeline you can't see inside</h3>
        <p>Revenue exists. Pipeline moves. But you can't tell where deals are stalling, what your Japan team is actually prioritizing, or which activities connect to outcomes.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <p class="card-num">03</p>
        <h3>Taking ownership of Japan or APAC revenue</h3>
        <p>You're new to the role. You've inherited a setup that wasn't designed for this market, or there is no setup at all. You need to fix what doesn't work and build something that doesn't depend on individual people.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== SERVICES（流れの図＋4つのレイヤー＋価格） ===================== -->
<section class="band band--grey">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Services</p>
      <h2>We connect the layers of Japan revenue execution.</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">From the first lead to renewal, across team lines, as one flow on one shared customer record. Most stalls happen at the handoffs between teams and in the data underneath.</p>
    </header>
    <RevenueFlowFigure id="en-flow" lang="en" label="Revenue flow" caption="Marketing, sales, and customer success as one flow. Points 1 and 2, and the data foundation, are where Japan pipelines usually stall." />

    <div class="card-grid card-grid--four">
      <a href="/en/services/revenue-architecture-design/" class="card card--link">
        <p class="card-num">Layer 1</p>
        <h3>Revenue Architecture Design</h3>
        <p>Define the revenue flow behind lead generation, lifecycle stages, ownership, handoff, and visibility.</p>
        <span class="card-cta">Learn more →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/services/japan-market-gtm-messaging/" class="card card--link">
        <p class="card-num">Layer 2</p>
        <h3>Japan GTM &amp; Messaging</h3>
        <p>Adapt positioning, messaging, offers, and conversion paths for Japan's buying context.</p>
        <span class="card-cta">Learn more →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/services/crm-revops-implementation/" class="card card--link">
        <p class="card-num">Layer 3</p>
        <h3>CRM / RevOps Implementation</h3>
        <p>Turn the model into CRM configuration, workflows, automation, and reporting.</p>
        <span class="card-cta">Learn more →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/services/adoption-growth-support/" class="card card--link">
        <p class="card-num">Layer 4</p>
        <h3>Adoption &amp; Optimization</h3>
        <p>Support launch, usage, and reporting habits until the system is part of daily execution.</p>
        <span class="card-cta">Learn more →</span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="price-summary">
      <h3>Investment range</h3>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Diagnosis</dt><dd>¥100K – ¥500K</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Redesign Project</dt><dd>¥3M – ¥8M</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Ongoing Retainer</dt><dd>¥300K – ¥1M / mo</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="price-summary__note">Prices exclude consumption tax.</p>
      <p class="price-summary__links"><a href="/en/services/">View all services →</a><a href="/services/">Full pricing (JA) →</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== REVENUE CRM（2本目の入口） ===================== -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="container product">
    <div class="product-copy">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Our Product</p>
      <h2>No CRM yet? Start with Revenue CRM.</h2>
      <p>Built from what 40+ CRM / MA / SFA implementations taught us about a CRM that gets used. No migration: start from what you already track in spreadsheets. AI suggests the next action, so it runs without adding headcount. English, Japanese, and Traditional Chinese UI.</p>
      <div class="product-links">
        <a href="/en/crm/" class="btn btn--cta">For B2B teams →</a>
        <a href="/en/crm/school/" class="btn btn--outline">For schools and coaching businesses →</a>
      </div>
      <p class="product-media">How-to guides and common problems: <a href="/en/crm/media/b2b/">B2B sales</a> / <a href="/en/crm/media/b2c/">schools</a></p>
    </div>
    <a href="/en/crm/" class="product-shot" aria-label="Revenue CRM dashboard. Go to the product page">
      <span class="product-shot__bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <img
        src="/images/crm/screen-dashboard-2026-10c-en.webp"
        alt="Revenue CRM dashboard: open pipeline, weighted forecast, win rate, overdue tasks, and an insights list with suggested next actions."
        width="1600"
        height="1000"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </a>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== CASE STUDIES ===================== -->
<section class="band band--grey">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Work</p>
      <h2>Selected case studies</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="card-grid card-grid--three">
      <a href="/en/case-studies/hubspot-sales-handoff-lead-to-revenue-2/" class="card card--link card--case">
        <div class="case-img">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/images/media/2026/02/dx.webp" type="image/webp" />
            <img src="/images/media/2026/02/dx.png" alt="Closing the Gap Between Lead Volume and Revenue" loading="lazy" width="700" height="394" />
          </picture>
        </div>
        <p class="card-num">HubSpot · Lead Operations</p>
        <h3>Closing the Gap Between Lead Volume and Revenue</h3>
        <dl class="case-dl">
          <dt>Problem</dt><dd>Lead volume was growing but revenue wasn't following. Handoff between marketing and sales was inconsistent.</dd>
          <dt>Work</dt><dd>Standardized lead scoring, defined handoff rules, and restructured pipeline stages with clear ownership in HubSpot.</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt><dd>Consistent lead-to-opportunity conversion with visible pipeline by source and stage.</dd>
        </dl>
        <span class="card-cta">Read case study →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/case-studies/https-consilegy-com-case-studies-ai-gtm-automation-product-integration/" class="card card--link card--case">
        <div class="case-img">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/images/media/2026/03/s-o-c-i-a-l-c-u-t-1RT4txDDAbM-unsplash.webp" type="image/webp" />
            <img src="/images/media/2026/03/s-o-c-i-a-l-c-u-t-1RT4txDDAbM-unsplash.jpg" alt="Building a Revenue Foundation for a New AI Business" loading="lazy" width="700" height="466" />
          </picture>
        </div>
        <p class="card-num">GTM · CRM Build</p>
        <h3>Building a Revenue Foundation for a New AI Business</h3>
        <dl class="case-dl">
          <dt>Problem</dt><dd>A new AI business needed a GTM foundation from scratch: no defined ICP, no CRM, no lead process, no messaging for Japan.</dd>
          <dt>Work</dt><dd>Defined ICP and Japan-specific messaging, built CRM from scratch with automation and lead flow design.</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt><dd>Operational revenue system in place to support the initial sales motion and measure early pipeline.</dd>
        </dl>
        <span class="card-cta">Read case study →</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/en/case-studies/marketing-data-integration-hubspot-migration-2/" class="card card--link card--case">
        <div class="case-img">
          <picture>
            <source srcset="/images/media/2026/02/apex-virtual-education-KNQUEQwTCY4-unsplash.webp" type="image/webp" />
            <img src="/images/media/2026/02/apex-virtual-education-KNQUEQwTCY4-unsplash-scaled.jpg" alt="Redesigning a Complex Marketing Stack" loading="lazy" width="700" height="394" />
          </picture>
        </div>
        <p class="card-num">HubSpot · Marketing Ops</p>
        <h3>Redesigning a Complex Marketing Stack</h3>
        <dl class="case-dl">
          <dt>Problem</dt><dd>Disconnected marketing tools made it impossible to track campaigns to revenue. Data was fragmented across systems.</dd>
          <dt>Work</dt><dd>HubSpot migration, data integration, and attribution model redesign to connect campaign activity to pipeline outcomes.</dd>
          <dt>Result</dt><dd>Unified marketing data with clear campaign-to-revenue visibility and a sustainable operating model.</dd>
        </dl>
        <span class="card-cta">Read case study →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="more-link"><a href="/en/case-studies/" class="btn btn--outline">View all case studies →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== WHY CONSILEGY ===================== -->
<section class="band">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="section-eyebrow">Why Consilegy</p>
      <h2>How we work differently</h2>
    </header>
    <ul class="why-list">
      <li><strong>We don't hand off.</strong> We stay engaged until execution works in practice, not just until delivery is complete.</li>
      <li><strong>Strategy and implementation in the same engagement.</strong> No gap between the plan and the system that's supposed to run it.</li>
      <li><strong>Japan-specific knowledge built in.</strong> Japan's buying process, approval dynamics, and trust expectations are part of the design from the start.</li>
      <li><strong>CRM designed around how Japan actually works.</strong> Stage definitions, handoff rules, and reporting are built around Japan's actual sales motion.</li>
      <li><strong>Bilingual without interpretation loss.</strong> We work directly with you in English and with your Japan team in Japanese, so nothing gets diluted between the two sides.</li>
      <li><strong>Our own product when you need one.</strong> If there is no CRM to fix yet, Revenue CRM, built from the same implementation lessons, is an option.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ===================== FINAL CTA ===================== -->
<section class="final-cta">
  <div class="container cta-inner">
    <p class="cta-eyebrow">Get Started</p>
    <h2>Japan revenue operations shouldn't be a black box.</h2>
    <p class="cta-lead">
      Whether your CRM needs a rebuild, your pipeline lacks visibility, or you are taking ownership of Japan or APAC revenue for the first time,
      we can help you design and implement the system that makes Japan execution work.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--cta-primary btn--lg">Contact Us</a>
      <a href="/en/services/" class="btn btn--cta-outline btn--lg">Explore Services →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* 日本語トップと同じ型：紺のFV（左右分割）・紺の帯・白とグレーの帯・白カード（紫の上線）・紫のCTA */
.container { max-width: 1160px; margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: 2rem; }
section { padding-block: var(--space-2xl); }
h2 { font-size: clamp(1.625rem, 2.4vw, 2.125rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.3; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--color-text); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
h3 { font-weight: 600; }
.section-eyebrow { display: block; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-text-muted); letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
.section-head { max-width: 720px; margin-bottom: var(--space-lg); }
.section-lead { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); line-height: 1.8; margin: 0; }

.btn { border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; }
.btn--lg { padding: 0.875rem 1.75rem; font-size: 1rem; }
.btn--cta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; background: #8758C9; color: #fff; border: 1px solid #8758C9; padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; transition: background 0.15s, border-color 0.15s; }
.btn--cta:hover { background: #6f45ad; border-color: #6f45ad; color: #fff; }
.btn--outline { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; background: transparent; color: var(--color-primary); border: 1px solid var(--color-primary); padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; }
.btn--outline:hover { background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06); color: var(--color-primary); }
